AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Madame Chair.
We are disappointed that the Commission was unable to adopt the Agreed Conclusions by consensus this year. The United States supported the overall agenda of this year’s CSW with its important focus on access to justice for women. W\and we arrived at this 70th Session, willing to negotiate and collaborate with all nations in the spirit of reaching consensus.
Leading up to CSW this year, the United States engaged in numerous discussions with the chair, co-facilitators, and other Member States. Despite clear communication of our redlines regarding “gender ideology” and “sexual and reproductive health and rights” among others, in the end our amendments were never brought to a formal vote.
And while our redlines were ignored, the United States Government will not stand by and watch as malicious forces misuse multilateral organizations to promote their ideologies and social agendas, obstructing nations’ abilities to exercise their national sovereignty. We will always protect women and girls from dangerous radical gender ideology and reaffirm biological truth.
Based on the final text of the Agreed Conclusions, the United States would like to clarify our positions on a few topics that prevented us from joining consensus and calling a vote.
Regarding “Gender”: It is the policy of the United States to recognize two biological sexes, male and female. To achieve this, we use clear and accurate language that recognizes women are biologically female and men are biologically male. Sex is not
interchangeable, rather it is irreplaceable. The differences between male and female should be celebrated, appreciated, and respected.
On “Sexual and reproductive health”: There has unequivocally never been an international commitment on “sexual and reproductive health and rights,” and we strongly oppose the use of this terminology. The Trump Administration is committed to supporting families, promoting women’s health, and protecting children at all stages of life and reaffirms there is no international right to abortion.
Thank you.
